B=r'''<style>.box p,.box li{font-size:20px;line-height:1.3}.box h2{font-size:23px;margin-bottom:4px}.tbl{font-size:17.5px}.note,.warn{font-size:17px}.tbl th,.tbl td{padding:2px 6px}.iq ol{font-size:19px;line-height:1.26}.pill{font-size:16px}.grid{gap:10px}.handle{bottom:-12px}.box{padding:9px 12px}.tagline{font-size:19px;margin-bottom:9px}.code{font-family:Consolas,'DejaVu Sans Mono',monospace;background:#f1f5f9;border:1px dashed #94a3b8;border-radius:6px;padding:5px 7px;margin:4px 0;line-height:1.3;font-size:15.5px;word-break:break-all}</style>
<div class="title">⏳ HxGN EAM Asynchronous Web Services <span class="badge">CHEAT SHEET</span></div>
<div class="tagline">New in 12.3: fire the request, get an ID back, let the server queue the work. (HxGN EAM Asynchronous Web Services brief, 12.3)</div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="box c1"><h2>1. Before 12.3: synchronous</h2><div class="flow" style="flex-wrap:wrap;row-gap:4px"><span class="pill">Client request</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Server runs it now</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Response</span></div><ul><li>Every EAM web service call ran <b>synchronously</b></li><li>Client waits for the full result</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c2"><h2>2. From 12.3: asynchronous</h2><ul><li>Server <b>queues</b> requests for later execution</li><li>Manages workload without immediate processing</li><li>Runs sync + async requests at more optimal levels</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c3"><h2>3. The async flow</h2><div class="flow" style="flex-wrap:wrap;row-gap:4px"><span class="pill">Client</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Web service tier</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">ASYNCWSID back</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Queue</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Asynchronous tier</span></div></div>
<div class="box c4"><h2>4. Cloud only ☁️</h2><ul><li>Async mode is available <b>exclusively in cloud</b> environments</li><li>On-premises: an async request is <b>treated as synchronous</b></li></ul></div>
<div class="box c5"><h2>5. What runs async</h2><ul><li>The <b>add interface transactions</b> web service is processed in asynchronous mode in cloud</li><li>A unique request ID, <b>ASYNCWSID</b>, comes back for tracking</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c6"><h2>6. Track the status</h2><div class="code">MP9577_GetAsynchronousWeb<br>ServiceRequestDetails_001</div><ul><li>Pass the <b>ASYNCWSID</b> to check status</li><li>Invalid ID = standard <b>invalid value</b> message</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c7"><h2>7. Sync vs Async</h2><table class="tbl"><tr><th></th><th>Sync</th><th>Async</th></tr><tr><td>Execution</td><td>Immediate</td><td>Queued</td></tr><tr><td>Client gets</td><td>Result</td><td>ASYNCWSID</td></tr><tr><td>Where</td><td>Cloud + on-prem</td><td>Cloud only</td></tr></table></div>
<div class="box c8"><h2>8. Client readiness</h2><ul><li>Some <b>client updating</b> may be needed first</li><li>So the client can receive and store the ASYNCWSID</li><li>Plan status checks into the integration design</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c1" style="grid-column:span 2"><h2>9. Sessions on the async tier (Octave Attune 12.3.1 release notes)</h2><ul><li>Since <b>12.3.0.2</b> the session used to submit AddInterface on the web service (axis) tier is <b>reused</b> on the async tier, so fewer sessions are created</li><li>SG-20010: NoSessionException seen on the async tier when SessionScenario is set to terminate</li><li>SG-18110: async PATCH asset requests reusing one session hit "IJ031050: The result set is closed"</li></ul></div>
<div class="bottom">
<div class="box" style="border-color:#1a5f7a"><h2 style="color:#1a5f7a">10a. Integration flow</h2><div class="flow" style="flex-wrap:wrap;row-gap:4px"><span class="pill">Submit</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Store ASYNCWSID</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Poll MP9577</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Act on result</span></div></div>
<div class="box iq"><h2>10b. Consultant tips</h2><ol><li>Test on cloud, not on-prem</li><li>Log every ASYNCWSID</li><li>Retest session handling after patches</li></ol></div>
<div class="box" style="border-color:#2d8a5a"><h2 style="color:#2d8a5a">10c. Key points</h2><ul><li>New in 12.3</li><li>Cloud only</li><li>ID = ASYNCWSID</li></ul></div>
</div></div>'''
